course: dictionary
lesson: 12295
title: A book of recipes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A cookbook is a book full of recipes. A recipe tells you which food to make, what to buy, and what to do step by step. The word has two parts, cook and book, and they give you the meaning. «Mum opened her cookbook to find a recipe for pancakes.»
explain: You can use a cookbook to make a meal one step at a time. «Sam followed the cookbook and made a chocolate cake all by himself.» The steps are in order, so you do one, then the next, and you do not skip any.
explain: The word can also mean any set of step-by-step instructions to follow, not only for food. Look at the clues: if the sentence talks about steps and following, it may mean instructions. «The cookbook says the recipe serves two, so double everything for four people.»
fact: A cookbook is a book of recipes and instructions for cooking.
fact: «Cookbook» is made from two words: cook and book.
fact: «Cookery book» means the same thing and is used in UK English.
fact: «Cookbook» can also mean any set of step-by-step instructions to follow (informal).
fact: Recipes in a cookbook can be scaled up or down by multiplying or dividing every amount.
exercise: «Mum opened her cookbook to find a recipe for pancakes.» What is a cookbook? | *A book of recipes and cooking instructions | A book about old castles | A map of the stars | A shop that sells bread
exercise: «Sam followed the cookbook step by step and made a cake.» What does step by step mean? | Without any help at all | *One step at a time, in order | Only the last step | Very quickly, skipping the steps
exercise: Ella wants to feed four people, but her cookbook recipe serves two. What should she do to the amounts? | Ignore the amounts | Use only one egg | *Double every amount | Halve every amount
test: «Grandad's cookery book is full of old family recipes.» What other word means the same as cookery book? | *Cookbook | Storybook | Notebook | Bookshelf
test: What is a recipe in a cookbook? | A type of pan for frying | A picture of a kitchen | *A set of instructions for making a food | A list of shops to visit
exam: Which of these is a cookbook? | A pan for boiling soup | A tin of soup | *A book of recipes for making soup | A spoon for stirring soup
